
---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Shivraj Deshmukh | Physics, Research, and Other Interests"
  description="My interests in theoretical physics, quantum gravity, AdS/CFT, bodybuilding, philosophy, and art."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container hero-grid">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow kicker">Research, notes, and other interests</span>

        <h1>Trying to understand gravity, and the universe it belongs to.</h1>

        <p class="hero-copy">
          I work on questions in
          <strong>quantum gravity, AdS/CFT, and theoretical physics</strong>.
          This site brings together my research and the other things that matter to me.
        </p>

        <div class="button-row">
          <a class="button" href={`${base}research/`}>
            Explore the research archive <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
          <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}about/`}>About me</a>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-note">Research comes first. There is more here, too.</div>

        <div class="personal-intro">
          <span class="eyebrow">A little about me</span>
          <p>
            I come from a farming family, and I want to do something worthwhile with the time
            I have. I want to understand as much of the universe as I can through physics and
            philosophy, while continuing to test myself through training and learning.
            I do not expect to have all the answers. I would like, in my own small way,
            to help us understand the universe a little better.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-art portrait-art">
        <div class="orbit-panel portrait-panel">
          <span class="hero-sticker">Physics<br />philosophy<br />life</span>

          <img
            class="portrait-image"
            src={`${base}images/shivraj-portrait.jpg`}
            alt="Portrait of Shivraj Deshmukh"
            loading="eager"
            fetchpriority="high"
          />

          <div class="orbit-caption">
            <span>Researcher / In progress</span>
            <strong>Still learning.<br />Still asking.</strong>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="container hero-bottomline">
      <span>Quantum gravity / AdS-CFT / High-energy theory</span>
      <span>Research · learning · life beyond physics</span>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="pale-blue-section">
    <div class="container pale-blue-grid">
      <div class="pale-blue-copy" data-reveal>
        <span class="eyebrow">Our place in the universe</span>

        <h2>We are a way for the cosmos to know itself.</h2>

        <p>
          Carl Sagan's words express an idea I find worth returning to: we are part of the
          universe we study. The atoms that make up our bodies formed through cosmic history,
          and we have developed the ability to investigate that history and ask questions
          about our own existence. For me, that is one reason learning about nature matters.
        </p>

        <span class="image-credit">Image credit: NASA / JPL-Caltech</span>
      </div>

      <figure class="pale-blue-figure" data-reveal>
        <img
          src="https://assets.science.nasa.gov/dynamicimage/assets/science/psd/photojournal/pia/pia23/pia23645/PIA23645.jpg"
          alt="Earth appearing as a tiny pale blue point in a beam of sunlight, photographed by Voyager 1"
          loading="lazy"
        />

        <figcaption>
          Earth, photographed by Voyager 1 from the outer Solar System on February 14, 1990.
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THEORETICAL PHYSICS VISUAL GALLERY -->
  <section class="physics-visuals">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="physics-heading" data-reveal>
        <span class="eyebrow">Ideas in theoretical physics</span>
        <h2>Black holes, holography, and the structure of spacetime.</h2>
        <p>
          I am interested in how gravity, quantum theory, geometry, and information fit
          together. The topics here approach that question in different ways, from the
          physics of black holes to the relationship between gravitational theories and
          quantum field theories.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="physics-grid">
        <article class="physics-card" data-reveal>
          <div class="physics-art black-hole-art">
            <img
              class="physics-photo"
              src="https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/vis/a010000/a013300/a013326/BH_Accretion_Disk_Sim_360_4k_Prores.00001_print.jpg"
              alt="NASA visualization of a black hole surrounded by a glowing accretion disk"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>

          <span class="physics-index">01 / GRAVITATION</span>
          <h3>Black holes</h3>
          <p>
            Black holes bring together strong gravity, spacetime geometry, and questions
            about what happens to information in quantum theory. Understanding them is
            an important part of the search for a quantum description of gravity.
          </p>
          <a
            class="physics-link"
            href="https://svs.gsfc.nasa.gov/13326"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >
            Explore the NASA visualization ↗
          </a>
        </article>

        <article class="physics-card" data-reveal>
          <div class="physics-art holography-art">
            <svg
              viewBox="0 0 320 210"
              role="img"
              aria-label="Conceptual illustration of information in a volume represented on its boundary"
            >
              <defs>
                <linearGradient id="holoVolume" x1="0" y1="0" x2="1" y2="1">
                  <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#d4e8df" stop-opacity="0.23" />
                  <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#88aebc" stop-opacity="0.04" />
                </linearGradient>
              </defs>

              <path d="M76 58 L181 31 L254 72 L148 103 Z" fill="url(#holoVolume)" stroke="#8cb7b1" stroke-width="1.5" />
              <path d="M76 58 L76 148 L148 184 L148 103 Z" fill="#9ac9bd" fill-opacity="0.1" stroke="#8cb7b1" stroke-width="1.5" />
              <path d="M148 103 L254 72 L254 160 L148 184 Z" fill="#83a9c2" fill-opacity="0.13" stroke="#8cb7b1" stroke-width="1.5" />

              <g stroke="#8cb7b1" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.65">
                <path d="M111 49 L183 89 L183 173" fill="none" />
                <path d="M147 40 L219 81 L219 168" fill="none" />
                <path d="M76 88 L148 126 L254 99" fill="none" />
                <path d="M76 118 L148 155 L254 129" fill="none" />
              </g>

              <g fill="#c74747">
                <circle cx="76" cy="58" r="3" />
                <circle cx="181" cy="31" r="3" />
                <circle cx="254" cy="72" r="3" />
                <circle cx="148" cy="103" r="3" />
                <circle cx="76" cy="148" r="3" />
                <circle cx="148" cy="184" r="3" />
                <circle cx="254" cy="160" r="3" />
              </g>

              <path d="M95 197 L225 197" stroke="#c74747" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" />
              <text x="160" y="206" fill="currentColor" font-size="9" text-anchor="middle">BOUNDARY / INFORMATION</text>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <span class="physics-index">02 / QUANTUM GRAVITY</span>
          <h3>The holographic principle</h3>
          <p>
            The holographic principle suggests that the information needed to describe
            a region of space may be encoded in degrees of freedom associated with
            its boundary. It changes how we think about space, gravity, and information.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="physics-card" data-reveal>
          <div class="physics-art ads-cft-art">
            <svg
              viewBox="0 0 320 210"
              role="img"
              aria-label="Conceptual diagram connecting a gravitational theory in a bulk space with a conformal field theory on its boundary"
            >
              <defs>
                <linearGradient id="adsBulk" x1="0" y1="0" x2="0" y2="1">
                  <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#9abdd5" stop-opacity="0.25" />
                  <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#9abdd5" stop-opacity="0.03" />
                </linearGradient>
              </defs>

              <path d="M37 165 Q160 17 283 165" fill="url(#adsBulk)" stroke="#9abdd5" stroke-width="2" />
              <path d="M56 165 Q160 45 264 165" fill="none" stroke="#9abdd5" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 5" />
              <path d="M78 165 Q160 72 242 165" fill="none" stroke="#9abdd5" stroke-width="1" stroke-dasharray="3 5" />

              <g stroke="#9abdd5" stroke-width="1" opacity="0.65">
                <path d="M160 40 L160 164" />
                <path d="M119 67 L119 164" />
                <path d="M201 67 L201 164" />
                <path d="M87 105 L87 164" />
                <path d="M233 105 L233 164" />
              </g>

              <path d="M37 165 Q160 196 283 165" fill="none" stroke="#c74747" stroke-width="3" />

              <g fill="#c74747">
                <circle cx="55" cy="169" r="3" />
                <circle cx="83" cy="177" r="3" />
                <circle cx="112" cy="183" r="3" />
                <circle cx="142" cy="186" r="3" />
                <circle cx="172" cy="186" r="3" />
                <circle cx="202" cy="183" r="3" />
                <circle cx="232" cy="177" r="3" />
                <circle cx="265" cy="169" r="3" />
              </g>

              <text x="160" y="19" fill="currentColor" font-size="11" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">BULK / GRAVITY</text>
              <text x="160" y="205" fill="currentColor" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="600">BOUNDARY / CFT</text>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <span class="physics-index">03 / GAUGE-GRAVITY DUALITY</span>
          <h3>AdS/CFT correspondence</h3>
          <p>
            AdS/CFT relates a gravitational theory in an anti-de Sitter bulk to a
            conformal field theory on its boundary. It provides a framework for studying
            gravity through quantum field theory, and vice versa.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="physics-card" data-reveal>
          <div class="physics-art entanglement-art">
            <svg
              viewBox="0 0 320 210"
              role="img"
              aria-label="Conceptual illustration of two quantum systems connected by entanglement correlations"
            >
              <defs>
                <radialGradient id="entangleGlow">
                  <stop offset="0%" stop-color="#c74747" stop-opacity="0.24" />
                  <stop offset="100%" stop-color="#c74747" stop-opacity="0" />
                </radialGradient>
              </defs>

              <circle cx="75" cy="101" r="48" fill="url(#entangleGlow)" />
              <circle cx="245" cy="101" r="48" fill="url(#entangleGlow)" />

              <path d="M75 101 C112 31 208 31 245 101 C208 171 112 171 75 101 Z" fill="none" stroke="#9abdd5" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-dasharray="4 5" />
              <path d="M75 101 C115 78 205 124 245 101" fill="none" stroke="#c74747" stroke-width="2" />
              <path d="M75 101 C115 124 205 78 245 101" fill="none" stroke="#c74747" stroke-width="2" opacity="0.75" />

              <circle cx="75" cy="101" r="27" fill="#18243a" stroke="#9abdd5" stroke-width="2" />
              <circle cx="245" cy="101" r="27" fill="#18243a" stroke="#9abdd5" stroke-width="2" />

              <g stroke="#f5f3ed" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round">
                <path d="M75 114 L75 88 M65 98 L75 88 L85 98" fill="none" />
                <path d="M245 114 L245 88 M235 98 L245 88 L255 98" fill="none" />
              </g>

              <text x="75" y="151" fill="currentColor" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle">SYSTEM A</text>
              <text x="245" y="151" fill="currentColor" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle">SYSTEM B</text>
              <text x="160" y="196" fill="currentColor" font-size="10" text-anchor="middle">QUANTUM CORRELATIONS</text>
            </svg>
          </div>

          <span class="physics-index">04 / QUANTUM INFORMATION</span>
          <h3>Quantum entanglement</h3>
          <p>
            Entangled quantum systems can have correlations that cannot be explained
            by assigning each system its own independent set of local properties.
            Entanglement also plays an important role in research on quantum information
            and the relationship between geometry and gravity.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="physics-card" data-reveal>
          <div class="physics-art wormhole-art">
            <img
              class="physics-photo"
              src="https://supernova.eso.org/static/archives/exhibitionimages/large/1209b-wormhole_cc.jpg"
              alt="Artist's concept from ESO showing a hypothetical wormhole connecting distant regions of space"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>

          <span class="physics-index">05 / SPACETIME</span>
          <h3>Wormholes</h3>
          <p>
            Wormholes are hypothetical spacetime geometries that could connect distant
            regions. They raise questions about the structure of spacetime and, in some
            theoretical settings, have interesting connections to quantum entanglement.
          </p>
          <a
            class="physics-link"
            href="https://supernova.eso.org/exhibition/images/1209b-wormhole_cc/"
            target="_blank"
            rel="noreferrer"
          >
            View the ESO illustration ↗
          </a>
        </article>
      </div>

      <p class="physics-disclaimer">
        These illustrations are schematic, not experimental images. The topics shown
        have different scientific status: black holes are supported by extensive
        observational evidence, while wormholes remain hypothetical. The holographic
        principle and AdS/CFT are theoretical frameworks studied in specific settings.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE DIFFERENT SIDES OF MY LIFE -->
  <section class="section tinted-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading" data-reveal>
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow kicker">Around this site</span>
          <h2>Physics is the centre. It isn't the whole picture.</h2>
        </div>

        <p>
          I spend a lot of time thinking about physics. Outside it, I train, read,
          write, make videos, take an interest in art, and try to understand people
          whose lives and ideas push me to think differently.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="area-grid">
        <a class="area-card" href={`${base}research/`} data-reveal>
          <div class="area-card-top">
            <span class="area-icon">∿</span>
            <span class="area-index">01 / CORE</span>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3>Research & academia</h3>
            <p>
              My work in theoretical physics: research projects, technical notes,
              derivations, papers, and presentations.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="area-card-bottom">
            <span>Explore research</span><b>↗</b>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a class="area-card" href={`${base}writings/`} data-reveal>
          <div class="area-card-top">
            <span class="area-icon">✳</span>
            <span class="area-index">02 / WORDS</span>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3>Writings & ideas</h3>
            <p>
              My own writing, notes on philosophy, ideas I am working through,
              and books or essays I have found worth spending time with.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="area-card-bottom">
            <span>Read my writing</span><b>↗</b>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a class="area-card" href={`${base}channels/`} data-reveal>
          <div class="area-card-top">
            <span class="area-icon">▷</span>
            <span class="area-index">03 / MEDIA</span>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3>Channels & media</h3>
            <p>
              The videos I make across my four YouTube channels, along with my
              Instagram presence and the different interests behind them.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="area-card-bottom">
            <span>Explore my channels</span><b>↗</b>
          </div>
        </a>

        <a class="area-card" href={`${base}art/`} data-reveal>
          <div class="area-card-top">
            <span class="area-icon">◒</span>
            <span class="area-index">04 / STUDIO</span>
          </div>

          <div>
            <h3>Art & photography</h3>
            <p>
              Photographs, paintings, visual experiments, and the creative side
              of life that doesn't need to become a research project.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="area-card-bottom">
            <span>View creative work</span><b>↗</b>
          </div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- BODYBUILDING, EXPLORATION, PHYSICS, AND CURIOSITY -->
  <section class="section personal-world">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading personal-world-heading" data-reveal>
        <div>
          <span class="eyebrow kicker">Outside the notebook</span>
          <h2>A few things that make me who I am.</h2>
        </div>

        <p>
          I like pursuits that ask something of you. Physics asks for patience and
          precision. Training asks for consistency. Exploring the world asks you to
          look beyond what you already know. None of these makes you an expert at life,
          but each can teach you something about how you approach it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="life-collage">
        <article class="life-image life-image-large" data-reveal>
          <img
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1534438327276-14e5300c3a48?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1200&q=85"
            alt="Weight-training gym with racks and training equipment"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="life-image-overlay">
            <span>01 / BODYBUILDING</span>
            <h3>Earn your progress.</h3>
            <p>Repetition, patience, and coming back when the excitement wears off.</p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="life-image life-image-mountain" data-reveal>
          <img
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1464822759023-fed622ff2c3b?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&q=85"
            alt="Mountain peaks rising into the clouds"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="life-image-overlay">
            <span>02 / EXPLORATION</span>
            <h3>Stay curious about the world.</h3>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="life-image life-image-space" data-reveal>
          <img
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1462331940025-496dfbfc7564?auto=format&fit=crop&w=900&q=85"
            alt="A colourful field of stars and distant nebulae"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="life-image-overlay">
            <span>03 / THE COSMOS</span>
            <h3>There is still so much to understand.</h3>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="life-image life-image-road" data-reveal>
          <img
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1470770841072-f978cf4d019e?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=85"
            alt="A road winding through a vast mountain landscape"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="life-image-overlay">
            <span>04 / THE LONG ROAD</span>
            <h3>Not everything has to happen quickly.</h3>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="life-note-card" data-reveal>
          <span class="life-note-mark">∞</span>
          <p>
            I come from a fairly ordinary beginning, but I don't want that to decide
            the limits of what I try to learn or do. I want to take my work seriously,
            keep challenging myself, and make the most of the opportunities I get.
          </p>
          <span class="life-note-signature">Still figuring things out.</span>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- PEOPLE AND IDEAS WORTH RETURNING TO -->
  <section class="section thinkers-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="thinkers-heading" data-reveal>
        <span class="eyebrow kicker">Words I keep coming back to</span>
        <h2>Curiosity, courage, and the work itself.</h2>
        <p>
          These aren't rules for living, and I don't agree with every famous person
          about everything. But certain lines stay with you because they put something
          difficult into words.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="thinkers-grid">
        <article class="thinker-card thinker-card-blue" data-reveal>
          <span class="thinker-field">PHYSICS & CURIOSITY</span>
          <span class="thinker-quote-mark">“</span>
          <blockquote>
            The important thing is not to stop questioning.
          </blockquote>
          <div class="thinker-credit">
            <strong>Albert Einstein</strong>
            <span>Keep asking why.</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="thinker-card thinker-card-red" data-reveal>
          <span class="thinker-field">SCIENCE & DISCOVERY</span>
          <span class="thinker-quote-mark">“</span>
          <blockquote>
            Somewhere, something incredible is waiting to be known.
          </blockquote>
          <div class="thinker-credit">
            <strong>Carl Sagan</strong>
            <span>There is more to discover.</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="thinker-card thinker-card-dark" data-reveal>
          <span class="thinker-field">EFFORT & COURAGE</span>
          <span class="thinker-quote-mark">“</span>
          <blockquote>
            The credit belongs to the man who is actually in the arena.
          </blockquote>
          <div class="thinker-credit">
            <strong>Theodore Roosevelt</strong>
            <span>From “Citizenship in a Republic”</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="thinker-card thinker-card-light" data-reveal>
          <span class="thinker-field">EXPLORATION</span>
          <span class="thinker-quote-mark">“</span>
          <blockquote>
            The only way of discovering the limits of the possible is to venture a little way past them into the impossible.
          </blockquote>
          <div class="thinker-credit">
            <strong>Arthur C. Clarke</strong>
            <span>On going beyond the familiar</span>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="thinker-card thinker-card-photo" data-reveal>
          <img
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1519681393784-d120267933ba?auto=format&fit=crop&w=1000&q=85"
            alt="A mountain beneath a star-filled night sky"
            loading="lazy"
          />
          <div class="thinker-photo-content">
            <span class="thinker-field">PERSPECTIVE</span>
            <p>
              We are small against the scale of the universe. That makes our questions
              no less worth asking.
            </p>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="thinker-card thinker-card-note" data-reveal>
          <span class="thinker-field">A PERSONAL REMINDER</span>
          <blockquote>
            Be ambitious about what you want to understand, and patient with how long it takes.
          </blockquote>
          <div class="thinker-credit">
            <strong>Not a quotation.</strong>
            <span>Just something worth remembering.</span>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- RETURN TO THE RESEARCH -->
  <section class="section research-invitation">
    <div class="container research-invitation-grid">
      <div data-reveal>
        <span class="eyebrow kicker">What brings me here</span>
        <h2>Back to the questions.</h2>
        <p>
          My central interest is theoretical physics, especially quantum gravity,
          AdS/CFT, and high-energy theory. I want to understand how the pieces fit
          together. That means working through the mathematics, checking the details,
          and being willing to find mistakes in my own calculations.
        </p>
        <p>
          This is the main purpose of the research section: a place for my actual work
          and the material I choose to share. I won't use sample papers or invented
          article titles to make the archive look fuller than it is.
        </p>
        <a class="button" href={`${base}research/`}>
          Go to the research archive <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="research-side-note" data-reveal>
        <span class="research-side-symbol">∿</span>
        <span class="eyebrow">The question behind the work</span>
        <p>
          Can we find a deeper description of nature that brings gravity and quantum
          theory together? If a unified picture exists, what would it take to understand it?
        </p>
        <span class="research-side-caption">A question, not a claim.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="closing-banner personal-closing">
    <div class="container closing-inner">
      <div>
        <span class="eyebrow">Still becoming</span>
        <h2>Learn seriously. Train hard. Stay curious.</h2>
        <p>
          There is a lot I don't know yet. That seems like a good reason to begin.
        </p>
      </div>

      <a class="button" href={`${base}about/`}>
        A little more about me <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <style is:global>
    .physics-visuals {
      padding: 5rem 0;
    }

    .physics-heading {
      max-width: 760px;
      margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
      text-align: center;
    }

    .physics-heading h2 {
      margin: 0.65rem 0 1rem;
    }

    .physics-heading p {
      max-width: 650px;
